# .rules

## Role
You are a Senior Frontend Engineer and Clean Architecture Specialist.

## Project: Fuel-Watch (Germany)
A Progressive Web App that displays real-time fuel prices from gas
stations across Germany. It provides price scoring based on daily
averages, golden hour analysis, weekly trend data, and supports
offline favorites with push notifications.

## Tech Stack
- Vite + React 18 + TypeScript (strict mode)
- Styling: Modern Vanilla CSS (Custom Properties, Flexbox, Grid)
  - Tailwind, Bootstrap, or any CSS framework is FORBIDDEN
  - CSS files must be co-located with their component
- i18n: No external library. Custom useTranslation hook + JSON files (DE/EN)
- APIs:
  - Tankerkönig (fuel prices) — requires API key in .env
  - Photon / photon.komoot.io (geocoding) — free, no key required
- State: React Context + useReducer (no Redux, no Zustand)
- Storage: LocalStorage for favorites and recent searches
- PWA: Custom service worker + manifest.json
- Deployment: Cloudflare Pages or Vercel (free tier, HTTPS required)
- Total cost: 0€

## Project Structure

    src/
      App.tsx              Root component (layout shell)
      main.tsx             Entry point (renders into DOM)

      api/                 API clients only. Pure HTTP calls.
        tankerkoenig.ts      Fuel price API (requires API key)
        photon.ts            Geocoding API (free, no key)

      core/                App-level infrastructure
        providers/           Context provider wrappers
        ErrorBoundary.tsx    Global React error boundary
        config.ts            Environment variable access
        sw-register.ts       Service Worker registration logic

      hooks/               Business logic layer
        useTranslation.ts    i18n with interpolation support
        useFuelStations.ts   Fetches stations via Tankerkönig
        useGeolocation.ts    Browser Geolocation API wrapper
        useGeocode.ts        City/PLZ to coordinates via Photon
        usePriceAnalysis.ts  Score calculation + golden hour
        useFavorites.ts      Read/write favorites to LocalStorage
        useRecentSearches.ts Read/write search history (max 5)
        useNotification.ts   Browser Push Notification wrapper

      locales/             Translation JSON files
        en.json              English translations
        de.json              German translations

      store/               Global state (Context + Reducer)
        LanguageContext.tsx   Current language state
        FavoritesContext.tsx  Favorite stations state
        SearchHistoryContext.tsx  Recent searches state

      styles/              Global CSS system
        reset.css            Minimal CSS reset
        variables.css        All design tokens
        global.css           Typography, layout, a11y utilities
        animations.css       Keyframe animations

      types/               Shared TypeScript definitions
        fuel.ts              Station, FuelType, FuelPrice
        geo.ts               Coordinates, PhotonResult
        analysis.ts          PriceScore, GoldenHour, TrendData
        storage.ts           FavoriteStation, RecentSearch

      ui/                  Presentational components only
        SearchForm/          City/PLZ input + fuel type + radius
        StationCard/         Station info + price + score badge
        ScoreBadge/          Visual score indicator
        Dashboard/           Main results layout
        TrendChart/          Weekly price trend (pure CSS bars)
        FuelTypeSelector/    E5 / E10 / Diesel toggle
        LanguageSwitcher/    DE / EN toggle
        Spinner/             Loading spinner
        Skeleton/            Content placeholder during loading
        ErrorMessage/        User-friendly error display
        InstallPrompt/       PWA install banner

      utils/               Pure helper functions (no side effects)
        formatPrice.ts       Number to "1,459 €/L"
        formatDistance.ts     Meters to "2.3 km"
        formatTime.ts        Timestamp to relative time string
        constants.ts         API URLs, defaults, thresholds
        scoring.ts           Price scoring algorithm
        goldenHour.ts        Optimal refueling time calculator
        weeklyTrends.ts      Static weekly data (ADAC source)
        storage.ts           Type-safe LocalStorage helpers

      workers/             Service Worker
        sw.ts                Cache strategy + push handler

## Architecture Rules
- api/: Only HTTP calls and response transformation. No business logic.
- hooks/: All business logic lives here. Components only call hooks.
- ui/: Pure rendering. Direct fetch or localStorage calls FORBIDDEN.
- types/: All shared interfaces and types. The "any" type is FORBIDDEN.
- utils/: Pure functions. No side effects. Must be unit-testable.
- store/: React Context + useReducer only. No external state libraries.
- core/: App-level concerns only (providers, error boundaries, config).
- workers/: Service worker only. No React code.

## Version Control
## Git Conventions
- Use Conventional Commits: <type>: <short description>
- Types: feat, fix, refactor, style, docs, chore, test, perf, a11y
- Each commit must represent exactly ONE logical change.
- Commit messages must be lowercase, max 72 characters.
- Do not bundle unrelated changes in a single commit.
- When asked for a commit message, analyze the git diff and suggest
  the appropriate type and description. If the diff contains multiple
  unrelated changes, recommend splitting into separate commits.

## Data Flow

    User Action -> ui/ component
      -> calls hook from hooks/
        -> hook calls api/ for data
        -> hook calls utils/ for transformation
        -> hook updates store/ if needed
      -> ui/ re-renders with new data

## API Constraints

### Tankerkönig API
- Polling frequency: MINIMUM 5 minutes between requests.
- Use list.php for nearby stations or prices.php for known station IDs.
- API key must come from VITE_TANKER_KEY environment variable.
- Graceful degradation: If throttled or offline, show user-friendly
  error message via UI. Never fail silently.

### Photon Geocoder API (photon.komoot.io)
- Use search-as-you-type pattern for location input.
- Limit results to 5 per query to respect demo server limits.
- No API key required.
- Filter results to Germany only (countrycode=DE parameter).

## Price Analysis Business Logic

### Scoring Algorithm (utils/scoring.ts)
- Formula: currentPrice - dailyAreaAverage
- If difference < -0.05 EUR: "Great Deal" (score 80-100)
- If difference is -0.05 to 0.00 EUR: "Fair Price" (score 50-79)
- If difference > 0.00 EUR: "Expensive" (score 0-49)

### Golden Hour Analysis (utils/goldenHour.ts)
- ABSOLUTE CHEAPEST window: 21:00 to 22:00 (saves 12-17 cents)
- BELOW AVERAGE window: 16:00 to 22:00 (saves 2-4 cents)
- MOST EXPENSIVE window: 05:00 to 07:00 (morning rush, +8 cents)
- These windows are based on 2026 ADAC research for Germany.

### Weekly Trends (utils/weeklyTrends.ts)
- Static dataset based on ADAC 2026 historical analysis.
- Cheapest days: Sunday and Monday.
- Data is used in TrendChart component (pure CSS bars, no chart library).

## Semantic HTML & Accessibility Rules
- Use semantic elements: <nav>, <main>, <article>, <section>, <header>, <footer>.
- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible (tabindex, role).
- ARIA labels must be used for non-semantic elements to provide context.
- Color contrast must meet WCAG AA standards (4.5:1 for normal text).

### Landmarks (index.html)
- The document MUST contain: <nav>, <main>, and a hidden <div> with
  aria-live="polite" for screen reader announcements.
- A skip-to-content link must be the first focusable element.

### Station Card
- Each station card MUST use an <article> element, not <div>.
- Price must be formatted for screen readers as spoken text:
  "One Euro eighty-one cents" not "1.81".
- Use aria-label on the <article> with full station context.

### Search Results Announcement
- When search completes, update the aria-live region with:
  "Found [N] stations, cheapest is [price] Euro"
- When no results, announce: "No stations found in this area"

### Focus Management
- All interactive elements must have visible focus rings.
- Tab order must be logical: Search -> Filters -> Results -> Favorites.
- Custom focus styles using box-shadow (not outline) for consistency.

## LocalStorage Rules
- Favorites: Store array of station ID strings. No size limit.
- Recent Searches: Store last 5 searches only. FIFO eviction.
- All storage operations must be wrapped in try-catch (private browsing).
- Use a version key for storage schema migration.

## Push Notification Rules
- NEVER request permission on page load.
- ONLY request after an explicit user gesture (clicking "Notify me").
- Notification content limits: headline < 50 characters, body < 200 characters.
- Trigger condition: If current time enters Golden Hour (21:00) AND
  user has at least one favorited station, fire a local notification
  with the cheapest price at their favorite station.

## PWA Service Worker Rules
- Pre-cache all critical assets: CSS, JS bundles, fonts.
- Network-first strategy for API calls (Tankerkoenig, Photon).
- Cache-first strategy for static assets (images, CSS, JS).
- App must load its UI shell even when completely offline.

## Performance Targets (Lighthouse)
- Performance: 90+
- Accessibility: 95+
- Best Practices: 95+
- SEO: 90+
- Bundle size: < 150KB gzipped (no heavy dependencies)

## Coding Standards
- Every function and component must have a JSDoc comment.
- Components use named exports only (default export FORBIDDEN).
- Props interface is defined in the same file as its component.
- CSS class names follow BEM: .station-card__price--cheap
- Error handling: try-catch with user-friendly messages from locales/.
- All variable and function names must be in English.
- File naming: camelCase for utilities, PascalCase for components.

## Component File Pattern
Each component in ui/ follows this structure:

    ui/
      StationCard/
        StationCard.tsx      Component logic
        StationCard.css      Scoped styles
        index.ts             Named re-export

## Response Format
- Add a brief English comment to every code line.
- When modifying a file, provide the COMPLETE file (partial snippets FORBIDDEN).
- After each step, suggest the logical "Next step".
- If a design decision is needed, present options and wait for approval.
- Keep explanations concise and structured.
- Always ensure that the code adheres to the defined architecture and rules.
- When adding new dependencies, justify their necessity and ensure they do not violate the "no heavy dependencies" rule.
- When asked to "create" or "scaffold" files, provide ONLY
  shell commands (mkdir/touch). Do NOT generate file contents
  unless explicitly asked with "write the code for [filename]".
- When asked to "refactor" or "modify" files, provide the COMPLETE
  modified file with comments. Do NOT provide diffs or partial snippets.
- Always maintain the integrity of the project structure and naming conventions.
- When asked to "explain" a piece of code, provide a concise summary of its purpose and how it fits into the overall architecture. Avoid lengthy explanations or tangential information.
